Tile 1 — Network Traffic (Total / In / Out) — 67 SCCM hosts
timeseries {
    traffic_in  = avg(dt.host.net.nic.bytes_rx, scalar:true),
    traffic_out = avg(dt.host.net.nic.bytes_tx, scalar:true)
  },
  by:{dt.entity.host},
  filter: dt.entity.host in [
    fetch dt.entity.host
    | filter arrayIndexOf(tags, "APMID:APP00005497") != -1
    | fields id
  ]
| fieldsAdd hostname = entityName(dt.entity.host)
| fieldsAdd traffic_total = traffic_in + traffic_out
| sort traffic_total desc
| fields hostname, traffic_total, traffic_in, traffic_out

Note

dt.host.net.nic.traffic (combined in+out) has no direct 1:1 Grail metric — only bytes_rx/bytes_tx are supported natively on Grail, per Dynatrace's own migration guide, so combining them ourselves (traffic_in + traffic_out) is the documented, correct approach, not a workaround.

🔍 Discovery Query — find the exact DNS query-time metric key
fetch metric.series
| filter contains(metric.key, "dns")
| summarize count(), by:{metric.key}
| sort metric.key asc
